{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"checkIsolated"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"externalID":"s:Scf13checkIsolatedyyF","title":"checkIsolated()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","platforms":[{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"name":"iOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"name":"iPadOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"name":"macOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false,"name":"tvOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"2.0","unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS"}],"required":true},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Last resort “fallback” isolation check, called when the concurrency runtime"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is comparing executors e.g. during "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Actor\/assumeIsolated(_:file:line:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and is unable to prove serial equivalence between the expected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(this object), and the current executor."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/checkisolated()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"checkIsolated"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"During executor comparison, the Swift concurrency runtime attempts to compare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"current and expected executors in a few ways (including “complex” equality"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between executors (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and if all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"those checks fail, this method is invoked on the expected executor."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method MUST crash if it is unable to prove that the current execution"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context belongs to this executor. At this point usual executor comparison would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have already failed, though the executor may have some external tracking of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"threads it owns, and may be able to prove isolation nevertheless."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A default implementation is provided that unconditionally crashes the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"program, and prevents calling code from proceeding with potentially"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not thread-safe execution."}]},{"style":"warning","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method must crash and halt program execution if unable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to prove the isolation of the calling context."}]}],"name":"Warning","type":"aside"}]}],"defaultImplementationsSections":[{"title":"SerialExecutor Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/checkIsolated()-76lg2"],"anchor":"SerialExecutor-Implementations"}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/SerialExecutor/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isSameExclusiveExecutionContext","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"other","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If this executor has complex equality semantics, and the runtime needs to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compare two executors, it will first attempt the usual pointer-based"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equality \/ check, \/ and if it fails it will compare the types of both"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executors, if they are the same, \/ it will finally invoke this method,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt to let the executor itself decide \/ if this and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"executor represent the same serial, exclusive, isolation context."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/SerialExecutor\/isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","defaultImplementations":2,"title":"isSameExclusiveExecutionContext(other:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/serialexecutor\/issameex